#import "common.typ": *

== 3. Combat Focuses
#columns(2, gutter: 6mm)[
=== 1. Never Leaves Anyone Behind
#quote(block: true)[
Loyal to a fault. You go back for the fallen, every time.
]

- #strong[Power tags:] #emph[I\'ve got your back];, #emph[carry them out]
- #strong[Weakness tag:] #emph[can\'t walk away]
- #strong[PC link:] \"I once failed to save someone. \[PC\] reminds me of them.\"

#figure(
  [#table(
    columns: (7%, 20%, 73%),
    align: (auto,auto,auto,),
    table.header([Tier], [Ability], [Effect],),
    table.hline(),
    [1], [#strong[Shield Bearer];], [When an ally next to you takes an imposed status, spend 1 point from any pool to reduce it by #strong[1 tier] before they Resist. This cannot reduce shared Disposition loss, injury-trade payments, running-dry statuses, agreed concession costs or other accepted payments.],
    [2a], [#strong[Second Wind];], [Once per scene, when you succeed on a Defend action while able to reach and assist a Taken Out ally, you may spend #strong[2 Power] to bring them back into the conflict. Reduce the status that took them out to #strong[tier 4];. They can participate again if their remaining conditions allow it, and rejoin your side\'s normal rotation without gaining an immediate turn. This does not reverse death or a settled defeat, remove other statuses or erase a Scar. The 2 Power buys this rescue instead of Disposition recovery; any remaining Power may restore Disposition normally.],
    [2b], [#strong[Interpose];], [When you accept an injury to cancel Disposition loss from an Attack or Feint, cancel #strong[1 additional] Disposition loss, up to the loss inflicted. All normal injury-trade restrictions apply.],
    [3a], [#strong[No One Left];], [Once per session, before a volley is revealed, declare a coordinated withdrawal. After that volley\'s actions finish, your side escapes the immediate conflict together, including Taken Out allies you can reach and carry. Give up the objective you were contesting unless it was solely to escape. The opposition achieves any compatible part of its declared intent, but cannot capture or separate the allies you extract. Apply no additional compromise. Existing injuries and paid costs remain. This grants no healing and does not recover allies already held elsewhere.],
    [3b], [#strong[★ Living Wall];], [Once per scene, until your next action, all imposed harm aimed at allies within reach that you can fictionally intercept hits you instead. Redirect it before the original target\'s Resistance or reduction; use your own eligible reduction. You Resist each with Edge +1. This does not redirect shared Disposition loss, injury-trade payments, running-dry statuses, agreed concession costs or other accepted payments. You cannot shield an ally from an area effect that already affects both of you.],
  )]
  , kind: table
  )

=== 2. Leads From the Front
#quote(block: true)[
Captain, chief, or sergeant: people follow you.
]

- #strong[Power tags:] #emph[born to command];, #emph[they believe in me]
- #strong[Weakness tag:] #emph[every loss is on me]
- #strong[PC link:] \"\[PC\] was the first person who ever followed my lead.\"

#figure(
  [#table(
    columns: (7%, 20%, 73%),
    align: (auto,auto,auto,),
    table.header([Tier], [Ability], [Effect],),
    table.hline(),
    [1], [#strong[Rally];], [Once per scene, spend 1 Momentum to restore #strong[2 points] to one pool of every ally who can hear you. This does not clear statuses, restore Disposition or erase Scars.],
    [2a], [#strong[Battle Plan];], [At the start of a conflict, the opposing side commits its first exchange\'s script. Before your side commits its own script, look at #strong[one] of those opposing actions. This grants no extra action and does not permit free changes after your own script is committed.],
    [2b], [#strong[Lead by Example];], [When you succeed with #strong[3+ Power];, the next ally who acts toward the same goal gets a #strong[free bonus die];. The normal bonus-dice cap applies; this grants no extra action.],
    [3a], [#strong[★ Warband];], [Gain a loyal crew (a group with 2 power tags and 1 weakness). It acts as one group, gives free Help once per scene, or holds a position. It takes statuses as a single target. If it acts independently in a conflict, it is one participant in your side\'s script and continuous rotation, and one participant for area-effect Disposition bonuses. It has no personal Disposition track or injury trade unless explicitly granted one. Free Help waives the pool-point cost, not relevance, bonus-dice limits or participation risks.],
    [3b], [#strong[Unbreak-able Line];], [Once per conflict, when your side\'s Disposition would drop to 0, it stays at #strong[1] and you take a tier-2 status as an accepted payment. Prevention, redirection, Resistance and incidental clearing benefits cannot cancel that payment; once recorded, it recovers normally. This does not increase starting Disposition or refresh an injury trade.],
  )]
  , kind: table
  )

=== 3. Masters a Weapon
#quote(block: true)[
Years of drill with one weapon: a blade, a rifle, a staff, bare fists.
]

- #strong[Power tags:] #emph[one with my \[weapon\]];, #emph[drilled every day]
- #strong[Weakness tag:] #emph[lost without it]
- #strong[PC link:] \"\[PC\] once saw me lose a duel, and kept it secret.\"

#figure(
  [#table(
    columns: (7%, 20%, 73%),
    align: (auto,auto,auto,),
    table.header([Tier], [Ability], [Effect],),
    table.hline(),
    [1], [#strong[Signature Style];], [Choose a weapon type. That weapon\'s tag may add #strong[+1 above the normal +2 cap (maximum +3 from tags)];, and it gains a second conflict action tag (e.g. a sword also gives +1 Defend).],
    [2a], [#strong[Riposte];], [In Fight conflicts, when you win a versus roll with Defend, you may spend any of that Power to remove the opposing side\'s Disposition instead of restoring your side\'s.],
    [2b], [#strong[Disarming Master];], [The Disarm maneuver costs #strong[2 Power] instead of 3. This sets its price to 2; another rule also setting it to 2 does not reduce it further. Outside conflicts, Weaken can strip an opponent\'s weapon tag for the scene.],
    [3a], [#strong[Perfect Strike];], [Once per scene, after rolling with your weapon, turn one kept die into a #strong[12];. If that creates doubles, apply them. Declare this before spending Power or applying the roll\'s consequences; it cannot reopen a settled outcome.],
    [3b], [#strong[★ Weapon Saint];], [Your weapon becomes an #strong[artifact] (Module A) with one extra power tag and an ability you design with the GM. It never depletes and costs no attunement Refresh.],
  )]
  , kind: table
  )

=== 4. Fights Dirty
#quote(block: true)[
Honour is for people who can afford to lose.
]

- #strong[Power tags:] #emph[no rules in a fight];, #emph[eye for a cheap shot]
- #strong[Weakness tag:] #emph[no one trusts me in a fair fight]
- #strong[PC link:] \"I taught \[PC\] that winning is the only thing that matters. They\'re still deciding if I was right.\"

#figure(
  [#table(
    columns: (7%, 20%, 73%),
    align: (auto,auto,auto,),
    table.header([Tier], [Ability], [Effect],),
    table.hline(),
    [1], [#strong[Cheap Shot];], [Once per scene, as part of an Attack, Create a story tag (#emph[sand in the eyes];, #emph[low blow];) for #strong[1 Power];. State the tag\'s scope and removal condition normally. This explicitly permits the Create purchase, not an additional scripted action or an automatic harmful status.],
    [2a], [#strong[Improvised Arsenal];], [Anything in reach is a weapon for you: chairs, bottles, tools. It gives #strong[+1 Attack or +1 Maneuver] and costs no load. This is an action tag, subject to normal relevance and the +2 tag cap unless an explicit exception applies; it is not additional Power or Disposition loss (Core Rules §2.1, §10.10).],
    [2b], [#strong[Kick Them While They\'re Down];], [Against a target with a harmful status of tier 2+, gain #strong[+1 Power] on Attack.],
    [3a], [#strong[Every Trick in the Book];], [In Fight conflicts, your successful Feints remove #strong[1 additional Disposition] when applying ordinary Feint Disposition loss. This is additional loss, not Power or a harmful status.],
    [3b], [#strong[★ Nothing Is Off-Limits];], [Once per session, declare a hazard Truth that was already there (#emph[gas leak];, #emph[rotten floor];, #emph[loose cargo];). Your next roll that uses it gets a #strong[free Extra Feat];. The declaration cannot contradict resolved events or retroactively recalculate Superiority. Free waives the Extra Feat\'s Power cost, not the action interaction or declared stakes; it grants no additional scripted action.],
  )]
  , kind: table
  )
]
